{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls7_jpg\\geo\\024.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "2.3 The Scarcity of Drinking Water in Cities", "conf": 0.88, "box": [[43, 81], [532, 75], [532, 102], [43, 108]]}, {"text": "The rapid urbanization that has been taking place in developing countries for the past few", "conf": 0.947, "box": [[43, 124], [804, 115], [804, 142], [43, 152]]}, {"text": "decadeshascreatedmanyproblemsforthepeopleliving incities.", "conf": 0.934, "box": [[44, 153], [564, 147], [564, 170], [44, 176]]}, {"text": "One of these problems is the scarcity of water. Most of the larger cities in the developing world", "conf": 0.926, "box": [[43, 183], [804, 174], [804, 200], [43, 209]]}, {"text": "are facing this problem. Themain reasons behindthis problemare:", "conf": 0.924, "box": [[43, 210], [572, 204], [572, 227], [43, 234]]}, {"text": "i). Climate change is causing decreased rainfall across many regions of the world and a", "conf": 0.929, "box": [[43, 242], [804, 232], [804, 257], [43, 266]]}, {"text": "reduction in rainfall means a reduction in the fresh water resources availablefor drinking.", "conf": 0.911, "box": [[42, 266], [751, 258], [752, 284], [42, 292]]}, {"text": "i). The ground surface of urban areas are invariably covered with concrete buildings and", "conf": 0.936, "box": [[43, 317], [803, 308], [803, 332], [43, 340]]}, {"text": "asphalt roads. This leaves very little bare ground to absorb rainwater, and without much", "conf": 0.927, "box": [[42, 341], [805, 333], [805, 359], [42, 367]]}, {"text": "rainwater absorption/seepage it becomes very difficult to recharge groundwater. When", "conf": 0.93, "box": [[43, 367], [805, 361], [805, 385], [43, 391]]}, {"text": "groundwater is not recharged, the water table begins to fall and people have a hard time", "conf": 0.914, "box": [[42, 391], [806, 383], [806, 410], [42, 419]]}, {"text": "accessing itfordomesticuse.", "conf": 0.912, "box": [[43, 419], [281, 416], [281, 438], [43, 441]]}, {"text": "ii).Lackofpropercityp